WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.452
Exercise 1: put your data under contract.

2
00:00:03.502 --> 00:00:09.376
Create the contract and open it in the Data Contract Editor.

3
00:00:09.427 --> 00:00:14.540
The editor opens with a new, empty contract. Set the fundamentals.

4
00:00:14.591 --> 00:00:19.874
Version 1.0.0 and status draft stay as they are. Save writes the YAML file to disk.

5
00:00:19.924 --> 00:00:28.212
Go to Servers and add the PostgreSQL database.

6
00:00:28.262 --> 00:00:38.098
Host localhost, port 5433, database workshop, schema orders_v1.

7
00:00:38.147 --> 00:00:43.382
Go to Schemas and add the orders table.

8
00:00:43.432 --> 00:01:03.319
Add the properties, each with a logical type and the physical type in the database.

9
00:01:03.369 --> 00:01:05.820
The other properties of orders and line_items follow the same way.

10
00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:15.384
Both tables, fully described. The Diagram view gives an overview.

11
00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:23.337
Test the contract against the real database. All checks pass.

12
00:01:23.387 --> 00:01:32.012
Change a physical type on purpose: the test catches the mismatch.

13
00:01:32.062 --> 00:01:39.717
customer_email_address is personal data: classify it as confidential.

14
00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:46.962
Mark it as required. The test then checks for missing values.

15
00:01:47.012 --> 00:01:53.582
Test again: required adds a check for missing values.

16
00:01:53.632 --> 00:02:01.504
Add a SQL quality check: every email contains an @.

17
00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:08.545
New in ODCS 3.2: context for AI agents. Open Context.

18
00:02:08.596 --> 00:02:14.722
A verified statement: a question with a curated SQL answer that agents should reuse.

19
00:02:14.773 --> 00:02:23.037
A constraint: what agents must never do.

20
00:02:23.088 --> 00:02:29.189
Add synonyms and lint the contract against ODCS 3.2.

21
00:02:29.239 --> 00:02:37.862
Add team, support, and SLAs, set the status to active, and test one last time.

22
00:02:37.912 --> 00:02:41.882
Tip: you can run the tests right in the editor, too.

23
00:02:41.933 --> 00:02:45.884
All checks pass: schema, types, and quality rules.

24
00:02:45.934 --> 00:02:48.884
Done. Next: data contract evolution.
